It is Thursday morning.
I am at the office.
Today I sit with Vikram.
Vikram is a software tester.
He tests our applications.
I go to his desk.
"Good morning Vikram," I say.
"Good morning Maya," he says.
He shows me his computer screen.
"I have prepared a test plan," Vikram says.
"I have found hundreds of bugs so far," he tells me with a laugh.
"I find mistakes in the code."
He opens a new file.
"I have written all the steps here," he says.
I read his plan.
He has done very good work.
"Thank you Vikram," I say.
"Your plan is very clear."
Now I am ready to write my code.
